From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 15:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/spacemit: inno_dp: guard shutdown/PM against unbound
 device

inno_dp_probe() only does component_add(); the struct soc_dp_dev is allocated
and platform_set_drvdata() + INIT_DELAYED_WORK() run later in the component
.bind callback (soc_dp_bind). The platform driver's .shutdown and system-sleep
PM callbacks, however, fire for the platform device regardless of whether the
component ever bound (e.g. headless K3 Pico-ITX with no DRM master up). In that
case platform_get_drvdata() returns NULL and the callbacks dereference it:

  cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dp->hpd_work)  with dp == NULL

so &dp->hpd_work is a tiny offset from NULL and timer_delete() faults, which on
the reboot path (systemd-shutdown, PID 1) turns into:

  Unable to handle kernel access ... at virtual address 0x1000
  inno_dp_shutdown+0x24 / cancel_delayed_work_sync / platform_shutdown
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Attempted to kill init!

Because nothing sets panic-on-reboot, the machine then hangs at the panic and
only recovers via the physical reset button - i.e. OS-initiated reboot/shutdown
never actually restarts the board.

Bail out early when drvdata is NULL in inno_dp_shutdown() and the four system
sleep PM callbacks (soc_dp_unbind is only reached after a successful bind, so it
is left untouched).

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/spacemit/spacemit_inno_dp.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/spacemit/spacemit_inno_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/spacemit/spacemit_inno_dp.c
@@ -3020,6 +3020,12 @@
 {
 	struct soc_dp_dev *dp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	/* .shutdown/PM callbacks fire even when the component never bound
+	 * (no DRM master); drvdata is then NULL and hpd_work etc. are
+	 * uninitialised. Bail out instead of dereferencing NULL. */
+	if (!dp)
+		return;
+
 #if HOT_PLUG_THREAD_ENABLED
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&dp->hpd_work);
 #endif
@@ -3033,6 +3039,9 @@
 	struct platform_device *pdev = to_platform_device(dev);
 	struct soc_dp_dev *dp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	if (!dp)
+		return 0;
+
 	DRM_INFO("%s()\n", __func__);
 
 #if HOT_PLUG_THREAD_ENABLED
@@ -3051,6 +3060,9 @@
 	struct platform_device *pdev = to_platform_device(dev);
 	struct soc_dp_dev *dp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	if (!dp)
+		return 0;
+
 	DRM_INFO("%s()\n", __func__);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dp->mode_lock);
@@ -3082,6 +3094,9 @@
 	struct soc_dp_dev *dp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!dp)
+		return 0;
+
 	DRM_INFO("%s()\n", __func__);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dp->mode_lock);
@@ -3109,6 +3124,9 @@
 	struct soc_dp_dev *dp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!dp)
+		return 0;
+
 	DRM_INFO("%s()\n", __func__);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dp->mode_lock);
